Originator(s):  amansnama
Date: Mon Nov 16 2026
Commit: 
One-line Summary: Split each crop into an untiled column and a tiled column using FTILE

Purpose of this version:
------------------------

FTILE on the surface dataset is the fraction of the grid cell that is tile-drained
(0 to 1, not a percent). The tiled share of the crop landunit is

    f = min(1, FTILE / crop fraction of the grid cell)

and each crop's columns are

    untiled   ctype = 2*100 + cft    weight = wt_cft * (1-f)    tile off
    tiled     ctype = 300 + cft      weight = wt_cft * f        tile on, full strength

A column whose weight is zero is not created (f of 0 or 1). The two weights sum to
the original wt_cft. Both patches keep the crop type and the full per-area fertilizer
rate. Natural vegetation is not split and is not drained.

TILE_DRAIN on the surface file is no longer read. tile_drain_everywhere still puts
the drain on every soil and crop column. do_transient_crops with FTILE > 0 stops at
startup; the dynamic-crop weight update still assumes one column per crop. pct_cft
diagnostics still keep one patch per crop. Not compiled or run.

Files:
  src/main/clm_varsur.F90            ftile(:)
  src/main/clm_initializeMod.F90     allocate and free ftile
  src/main/surfrdMod.F90             read FTILE
  src/main/subgridMod.F90            count one or two columns per crop
  src/main/initGridCellsMod.F90      build the two columns
  src/main/initVerticalMod.F90       tile_active from column type 300+cft
  src/main/column_varcon.F90         300+cft helpers and history metadata
  src/main/ColumnType.F90            column-type comment

Builds and runs OK.

