Tag name:  clm5-TileDrain (on top of the separate tile and surface nitrate fields)
Originator(s):  amansnama
Date: Mon Nov 16 2026
Commit: 7df9799
One-line Summary: Take tile-drain nitrate at the bulk column concentration (default); keep the layer scheme as an option

Purpose of this version:
------------------------

The tile nitrate was taken only from the layers the tile removed water from (at and
above the drain), at each layer's own dissolved NO3 concentration. CLM has no vertical
nitrate transport, so nitrate stays where it is made and is used up in the top of the
soil. In a 1Pt run with a 7 m drain the nitrate at the drain depth was about 1e-19
gN/m3 (6.8 gN/m3 at 1 cm), so SMIN_NO3_TILE was about 4.6e-22 gN/m2/yr (exactly 0 in
many months) while QTILE was about 125 mm/yr and SMIN_NO3_SURF was 0.27 gN/m2/yr. The
tile had no nitrate to remove, whatever its geometry or the fertilizer rate.

tile_no3_scheme selects how the tile picks up nitrate. Default is bulk.

  bulk (default):
     The tile water carries the bulk dissolved NO3 concentration of the whole soil
     column, in the same form as nitrate leached with subsurface drainage:
        smin_no3_leached_vr = disn_conc * qflx_drain * h2osoi_liq / (tot_water * dz)
        no3_tile            = disn_conc * qflx_tile  * h2osoi_liq / (tot_water * dz)
     disn_conc = sf_no3 * smin_no3_vr * dz / h2osoi_liq (gN/kg water), tot_water is
     the liquid water summed over nlevsoi, and qflx_tile is the column total (not
     qflx_tile_vr). Each layer loses its share in proportion to its liquid water.
     Summed over the column this is qflx_tile times the column-mean dissolved NO3.
     The result is zero if qflx_tile is zero (no tile drain), or tot_water is zero.

  layer (previous implementation):
     no3_tile = disn_conc * qflx_tile_vr / dz. Taken only from the layers the tile
     removed water from, in proportion to the water removed from each.

  Unchanged for both: the same pool limit (runoff <= smin_no3_vr/dt minus leaching),
  the same split into SMIN_NO3_TILE and SMIN_NO3_SURF with the cut taken from the
  tile term first, SMIN_NO3_SURF + SMIN_NO3_TILE = SMIN_NO3_RUNOFF, and
  Flrl_no3_runoff as the gridcell average of SMIN_NO3_RUNOFF. The tile water flux,
  QTILE, QDRAI and all hydrology are unchanged.

Summary of changes:
-------------------

Science changes:
  - New default: tile_no3_scheme = 'bulk'. Runs that use tile drainage with
    use_nitrif_denitrif and use_vertsoilc get a larger SMIN_NO3_TILE and
    SMIN_NO3_RUNOFF, and so a smaller nitrate pool and a larger nitrate flux to the
    river model, than with the previous code.
  - 'layer' reproduces the previous tile nitrate. It is bit-for-bit with the
    previous code, because only the one expression for no3_tile differs.
  - Without use_tile_drain qflx_tile is zero, so there is no change for either value.
  - With bulk, a layer can lose tile nitrate even if the tile removed no water
    from it. SMIN_NO3_TILE_vr is therefore no longer a map of where the tile took
    its water. The pool limit still keeps every layer non-negative.

Software changes:
  - SoilBiogeochemNLeachingMod: reads qflx_tile_col (column total) as well as
    qflx_tile_vr_col. New local tile_no3_bulk set from tile_no3_scheme; no3_tile
    follows the chosen scheme. Uses tile_no3_scheme from clm_varctl.
  - clm_varctl: new tile_no3_scheme (character(len=16), default 'bulk').
  - controlMod: new namelist item in clm_inparm, converted to lower case, checked
    (must be bulk or layer), broadcast, and printed in the log when use_tile_drain
    is true.
  - CLMBuildNamelist.pm: adds the default whenever use_tile_drain is true.
  - namelist_definition_clm4_5.xml (new entry, valid values bulk,layer, and the
    QTILE entry no longer says the nitrate is taken only from the drained layers),
    namelist_defaults_clm4_5.xml (bulk).

Changes to User Interface:
  New namelist item (group clm_inparm), used only if use_tile_drain = .true. and
  use_nitrif_denitrif and use_vertsoilc are on:
     tile_no3_scheme = 'bulk'    (or 'layer' for the previous behaviour)
  A case built before this change has to be rebuilt and have preview_namelists run
  again for the item to reach its namelist. To repeat an earlier run, add
     tile_no3_scheme = 'layer'
  to user_nl_clm.

Testing: The XML files parse and CLMBuildNamelist.pm passes perl -c. Builds and runs.

Known limits:
  - bulk makes up for the lack of vertical nitrate transport; it does not add it.
    The physically consistent fix is to move dissolved NO3 down with the water flux.
  - bulk uses the whole column up to nlevsoi, not only the soil above the drain.
  - No change for the non-vertically-resolved branch (use_vertsoilc = .false.),
    which still sets the tile and surface nitrate to zero.

