Commit: 8b50efd548cc874bfcd79c16d9efd09f74d0b04e
One-line Summary: Write tile-drain and surface-runoff nitrate to their own history fields

Purpose of this version:
------------------------

The nitrate carried by tile drainage was only recorded inside SMIN_NO3_RUNOFF, added
to the surface-runoff term. It is now also stored on its own, without changing the
runoff flux or the nitrate sent to the river model.

  SMIN_NO3_LEACHED  follows QDRAI. Tile water is not in it.
  SMIN_NO3_RUNOFF   is surface runoff (QOVER, top 5 cm) plus the tile term.
  SMIN_NO3_SURF     is the surface-runoff part of SMIN_NO3_RUNOFF (no3_runoff_surf
                    after the pool limit).
  SMIN_NO3_TILE     is the tile part of SMIN_NO3_RUNOFF. If the pool limit cuts
                    the sum, the cut is taken from the tile term first.
  SMIN_NO3_SURF + SMIN_NO3_TILE = SMIN_NO3_RUNOFF. Flrl_no3_runoff is still the
  gridcell average of SMIN_NO3_RUNOFF.

Both new fields are on the primary history tape when use_nitrif_denitrif is true
(gN/m^2/s). The _vr fields are registered but inactive. They are not new
nitrogen-balance terms.

Software changes:
  SoilBiogeochemNitrogenFluxType: smin_no3_tile_vr_col, smin_no3_tile_col,
  smin_no3_surf_vr_col, smin_no3_surf_col.
  SoilBiogeochemNLeachingMod: both parts are saved after the runoff pool limit.

Testing: Builds and runs at 1Pt. All previous tests were also in 1Pt mode.

